  body: "# Entitlement decision supporting overpayment recovery\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe chapter describes
    a valid revision or supersession decision before or alongside an overpayment recoverability decision, with stated
    exceptions.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nDMG 09026 and 09032 prevent treating the introductory requirement
    as universal. The period must be covered correctly and the award-versus-payment distinction retained. This is
    not an executable recovery sequence.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 09023, PDF page 4](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/678776493a9388161c5d23d5/dmgch09.pdf#page=4)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 9: Overpayments, offsets and recoverability.\n- [DMG 09026, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/678776493a9388161c5d23d5/dmgch09.pdf#page=5)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 9: Overpayments, offsets and recoverability.\n- [DMG 09030, PDF page 6](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/678776493a9388161c5d23d5/dmgch09.pdf#page=6)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 9: Overpayments, offsets and recoverability.\n- [DMG 09032, PDF page 6](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/678776493a9388161c5d23d5/dmgch09.pdf#page=6)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 9: Overpayments, offsets and recoverability.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted
    interpretation of the 15 September 2026 source snapshot; unreviewed and requiring specialist review. The source
    is DWP guidance, not a consolidated statement of legislation. This is an independent experimental publication,
    not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule.\n\nPDF page numbers are
    one-based file positions. Machine extraction can alter reading order, footnotes and characters. Quoted relationships
    preserve extracted text; no visual or specialist acceptance is claimed. Source dates, legal effects and current
    applicability remain separate review tasks.\n\n- `dmg-vol3-ch9` PDF SHA-256: `96933fc64fcacb0a3e253a686218757a85fb415574fde11e4d3435149b1a2505`;
    extracted pages SHA-256: `069cefdb6e8a7486021d251c6991ef627fc063a3b842eff2e98cde688ed831d2`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/dmg-revision
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source names revision as one route for the supporting entitlement decision; the recorded
      exceptions qualify the general requirement.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol3-ch9/0004
      quote: "09023 The following guidance deals with the requirement for a valid revision or supersession decision
        to\nbe made before, or at the same time that an overpayment recoverability decision is made.\n\n\nNote:
        Further guidance on revision is in DMG Chapter 03. Further guidance on supersession is in DMG\nChapter 04."
      locator: DMG 09023
    - page: page/dmg-vol3-ch9/0005
      quote: "09026 There are exceptions to the general rule at DMG 09025. These are\n\n\n1. where the facts and
        circumstances of the misrepresentation or the failure to disclose do not provide a\n\nbasis for revising
        or superseding the decision1 (see DMG 09032) or\n\n\n2. certain JSA overpayments to 16/17 year olds2 (see
        DMG 09295 - 09300).\n\n\n                                                                   1 SS (POR) Regs,
        reg 12; 2 SS A Act, s 71A"
      locator: DMG 09026
  - target: term/dmg-supersession
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: Supersession is the alternative route explicitly named in the same requirement; no equivalence
